window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b246-81a80fdbcbb5c732.json"]={sha256:"81a80fdbcbb5c732db802b98e98443864039d24a50b7778c027a194cd12be515",value:{"id":"b246","title":"階梯式溢洪道","titleEn":"Stepped spillways","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以以階梯流態含氣與剩餘能量驗證陡槽性能為主線，先用臨界水深與單寬流量與階高與相對尺度界定水力與構造條件，再將自含氣起點判讀、近壁低壓與氣蝕連結到縮尺黏性與可比性。以矩形斷面及均勻混合近似作示意，流態分界與氣蝕風險須依專案試驗。 每單元以原創算例、量測與失效辨識共同檢查推論。","summaryEn":"This course develops verifying stepped-chute regimes aeration and residual energy through Critical depth and unit discharge and Step height and relative scale, then connects Self-aeration inception identification and Near-wall pressure and cavitation to Scale viscosity and comparability. Rectangular sections and uniform-mixture approximations illustrate behavior; regime boundaries and cavitation require project testing. Each unit combines original calculation, measurement and failure diagnosis to test the inference.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-hydraulics","subcategoryTitle":"壩工監測、溢洪與壓力水路","subcategoryTitleEn":"Dam monitoring, spillways and pressure waterways","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-hydraulics","learningTags":["water","water-hydraulics","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-hydraulic","architectureNodes":[["臨界水深與單寬流量","Critical depth and unit discharge"],["階梯坡度與建造","Step geometry and construction"],["自含氣起點判讀","Self-aeration inception identification"],["近壁低壓與氣蝕","Near-wall pressure and cavitation"],["縮尺黏性與可比性","Scale viscosity and comparability"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[0,3]],"diagram":{"type":"water-hydraulic","labels":["臨界水深與單寬流量","階梯坡度與建造","自含氣起點判讀","近壁低壓與氣蝕","縮尺黏性與可比性"],"labelsEn":["Critical depth and unit discharge","Step geometry and construction","Self-aeration inception identification","Near-wall pressure and cavitation","Scale viscosity and comparability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合算例輸入全為教學假設，先檢查臨界水深與單寬流量：q=4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; criticalDepth=(4**2/9.81)**(1/3)=1.17711 m；再獨立檢查階高與相對尺度：criticalDepth=1.2 m; stepHeight=0.6 m; relativeDepth=1.2/0.6=2 dimensionless。敏感度：單寬流量由4增至6m2/s時，臨界水深由1.177增為1.542m，增加31.0%；若階高不變，水深階高比隨之提高，但不能用此一比值作通用流態界線。 兩個結果須按各自量綱解釋，不能直接相加或當成完整設計。以矩形斷面及均勻混合近似作示意，流態分界與氣蝕風險須依專案試驗。 將比較槽末清水等效比能與消能池入流工況表作為獨立驗證，明確列出尚缺的現地輸入及其對結論的影響。","textEn":"Every input in this integrated example is a teaching assumption. First examine Critical depth and unit discharge: q=4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; criticalDepth=(4**2/9.81)**(1/3)=1.17711 m. Independently examine Step height and relative scale: criticalDepth=1.2 m; stepHeight=0.6 m; relativeDepth=1.2/0.6=2 dimensionless. Sensitivity: raising unit discharge from4 to6m2/s increases critical depth from1.177 to1.542m, about31.0 percent. At fixed step height the relative depth rises, but this ratio alone is not a universal regime boundary. Interpret each result in its own dimensions rather than adding them or treating them as a complete design. Rectangular sections and uniform-mixture approximations illustrate behavior; regime boundaries and cavitation require project testing. Use the following independent check: Compare terminal clear-water equivalent energy with basin approach-condition tables. Identify missing field inputs and state which conclusions depend on them.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b246-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「臨界水深與單寬流量」與「階高與相對尺度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Critical depth and unit discharge\" and \"Step height and relative scale\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b246-v15-01","title":"臨界水深與單寬流量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Critical depth and unit discharge: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「臨界水深與單寬流量」如何影響階梯式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Critical depth and unit discharge” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stepped spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"階梯流態與流量相對階高有關，先以單寬流量求矩形明渠的臨界水深可建立尺度。此水深不是階面實際平均水深，也不是含氣混合水深；橫向不均流與入口曲率會改變局部條件，需另外量測入口過渡區。 驗證時應以全寬流量積分核對單寬值並標記階高與入口幾何，並辨識以下失效情境：把含氣厚度當臨界水深會混淆流態尺度。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「臨界水深與單寬流量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Critical depth based on unit discharge supplies a reference scale for stepped-flow behavior. It is neither the actual mean depth above a step nor the aerated mixture depth. Transverse nonuniformity and entrance curvature alter local conditions and require measurements through the crest transition. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Check unit discharge by full-width integration and record step height and entrance geometry. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Using aerated thickness as critical depth confuses the regime scale. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Critical depth and unit discharge” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：q=4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; criticalDepth=(4**2/9.81)**(1/3)=1.17711 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: q=4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; criticalDepth=(4**2/9.81)**(1/3)=1.17711 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「臨界水深就是每一階上的實際水深」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Critical depth equals actual flow depth on every step\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「臨界水深與單寬流量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Critical depth and unit discharge”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-01-k1","title":"臨界水深與單寬流量","titleEn":"Critical depth and unit discharge","text":"階梯流態與流量相對階高有關，先以單寬流量求矩形明渠的臨界水深可建立尺度。此水深不是階面實際平均水深，也不是含氣混合水深；橫向不均流與入口曲率會改變局部條件，需另外量測入口過渡區。","textEn":"Critical depth based on unit discharge supplies a reference scale for stepped-flow behavior. It is neither the actual mean depth above a step nor the aerated mixture depth.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：臨界水深就是每一階上的實際水深 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Critical depth equals actual flow depth on every step Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「臨界水深與單寬流量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Critical depth and unit discharge\" is correct?","options":["臨界水深就是每一階上的實際水深","階梯流態與流量相對階高有關，先以單寬流量求矩形明渠的臨界水深可建立尺度。","同一水深階高比保證所有坡度流態相同"],"optionsEn":["Critical depth equals actual flow depth on every step","Critical depth based on unit discharge supplies a reference scale for stepped-flow behavior.","The same relative depth guarantees the same regime on every slope"],"answer":1,"explanation":"階梯流態與流量相對階高有關，先以單寬流量求矩形明渠的臨界水深可建立尺度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Critical depth based on unit discharge supplies a reference scale for stepped-flow behavior. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b246-v15-02","title":"臨界水深與單寬流量：定量估算","titleEn":"Critical depth and unit discharge: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「臨界水深與單寬流量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Critical depth and unit discharge” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：q=4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; criticalDepth=(4**2/9.81)**(1/3)=1.17711 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: q=4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; criticalDepth=(4**2/9.81)**(1/3)=1.17711 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以全寬流量積分核對單寬值並標記階高與入口幾何。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check unit discharge by full-width integration and record step height and entrance geometry.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：q=4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; criticalDepth=(4**2/9.81)**(1/3)=1.17711 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: q=4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; criticalDepth=(4**2/9.81)**(1/3)=1.17711 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「臨界水深與單寬流量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Critical depth and unit discharge\", which statement holds?","options":["只要增加階數總耗能就能無限制線性增加","混合層厚度與清水等效深度永遠相同","原創教學假設：q=4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; criticalDepth=(4**2/9.81)**(1/3)=1.17711 m。"],"optionsEn":["Adding steps increases total dissipation linearly without limit","Mixture thickness always equals clear-water equivalent depth","Original teaching assumptions: q=4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; criticalDepth=(4**2/9.81)**(1/3)=1.17711 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：q=4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; criticalDepth=(4**2/9.81)**(1/3)=1.17711 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: q=4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; criticalDepth=(4**2/9.81)**(1/3)=1.17711 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b246-v15-03","title":"臨界水深與單寬流量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Critical depth and unit discharge: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「臨界水深與單寬流量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Critical depth and unit discharge” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以全寬流量積分核對單寬值並標記階高與入口幾何。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把含氣厚度當臨界水深會混淆流態尺度」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check unit discharge by full-width integration and record step height and entrance geometry. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Using aerated thickness as critical depth confuses the regime scale. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以全寬流量積分核對單寬值並標記階高與入口幾何作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把含氣厚度當臨界水深會混淆流態尺度，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check unit discharge by full-width integration and record step height and entrance geometry. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Using aerated thickness as critical depth confuses the regime scale. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：把含氣厚度當臨界水深會混淆流態尺度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using aerated thickness as critical depth confuses the regime scale. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以全寬流量積分核對單寬值並標記階高與入口幾何。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把含氣厚度當臨界水深會混淆流態尺度」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Check unit discharge by full-width integration and record step height and entrance geometry. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Using aerated thickness as critical depth confuses the regime scale. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以全寬流量積分核對單寬值並標記階高與入口幾何作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把含氣厚度當臨界水深會混淆流態尺度，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check unit discharge by full-width integration and record step height and entrance geometry. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Using aerated thickness as critical depth confuses the regime scale. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「臨界水深與單寬流量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Critical depth and unit discharge\"?","options":["以全寬流量積分核對單寬值並標記階高與入口幾何。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","有階梯溢洪道就一定不需要末端消能"],"optionsEn":["Check unit discharge by full-width integration and record step height and entrance geometry.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Every stepped spillway eliminates the need for terminal dissipation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"以全寬流量積分核對單寬值並標記階高與入口幾何。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check unit discharge by full-width integration and record step height and entrance geometry. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b246-v15-04","title":"臨界水深與單寬流量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Critical depth and unit discharge: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「臨界水深與單寬流量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Critical depth and unit discharge” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把含氣厚度當臨界水深會混淆流態尺度。診斷時應採取以下查核：以全寬流量積分核對單寬值並標記階高與入口幾何，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using aerated thickness as critical depth confuses the regime scale. Diagnose it by the following check: Check unit discharge by full-width integration and record step height and entrance geometry. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「臨界水深就是每一階上的實際水深」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Critical depth equals actual flow depth on every step\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把含氣厚度當臨界水深會混淆流態尺度。診斷時應採取以下查核：以全寬流量積分核對單寬值並標記階高與入口幾何，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Using aerated thickness as critical depth confuses the regime scale. Diagnose it by the following check: Check unit discharge by full-width integration and record step height and entrance geometry. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「臨界水深與單寬流量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Critical depth and unit discharge\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把含氣厚度當臨界水深會混淆流態尺度。","同一水深階高比保證所有坡度流態相同"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Using aerated thickness as critical depth confuses the regime scale.","The same relative depth guarantees the same regime on every slope"],"answer":1,"explanation":"把含氣厚度當臨界水深會混淆流態尺度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using aerated thickness as critical depth confuses the regime scale. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b246-v15-05","title":"階高與相對尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Step height and relative scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「階高與相對尺度」如何影響階梯式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Step height and relative scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stepped spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"階高改變水流是否逐階跌落或掠過階尖，水深階高比可整理試驗但還需陡槽坡度與入口邊界。過渡流態可能出現不規則噴濺與波動；不能把某一試驗的分界數值直接當成所有坡度皆適用的設計限制。 驗證時應在連續變流量試驗中記錄水舌是否撞擊階面及流態轉換，並辨識以下失效情境：只測單一流量會漏掉過渡流態的不規則噴濺。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「階高與相對尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Step height influences whether water cascades between steps or skims over their tips. A relative-depth ratio organizes experiments but slope and entrance conditions also matter. Transitional flow may splash irregularly; a boundary observed in one experiment is not a universal design limit across slopes. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Record nappe impact and regime transitions during a continuous discharge sweep. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Testing one discharge can miss irregular splashing in transitional flow. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Step height and relative scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：criticalDepth=1.2 m; stepHeight=0.6 m; relativeDepth=1.2/0.6=2 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: criticalDepth=1.2 m; stepHeight=0.6 m; relativeDepth=1.2/0.6=2 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「同一水深階高比保證所有坡度流態相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The same relative depth guarantees the same regime on every slope\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「階高與相對尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Step height and relative scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-05-k1","title":"階高與相對尺度","titleEn":"Step height and relative scale","text":"階高改變水流是否逐階跌落或掠過階尖，水深階高比可整理試驗但還需陡槽坡度與入口邊界。過渡流態可能出現不規則噴濺與波動；不能把某一試驗的分界數值直接當成所有坡度皆適用的設計限制。","textEn":"Step height influences whether water cascades between steps or skims over their tips. A relative-depth ratio organizes experiments but slope and entrance conditions also matter.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：同一水深階高比保證所有坡度流態相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The same relative depth guarantees the same regime on every slope Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「階高與相對尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Step height and relative scale\" is correct?","options":["同一水深階高比保證所有坡度流態相同","平均坡度正確就不必檢查個別階梯","階高改變水流是否逐階跌落或掠過階尖，水深階高比可整理試驗但還需陡槽坡度與入口邊界。"],"optionsEn":["The same relative depth guarantees the same regime on every slope","Correct average slope removes the need to inspect individual steps","Step height influences whether water cascades between steps or skims over their tips."],"answer":2,"explanation":"階高改變水流是否逐階跌落或掠過階尖，水深階高比可整理試驗但還需陡槽坡度與入口邊界。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Step height influences whether water cascades between steps or skims over their tips. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b246-v15-06","title":"階高與相對尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Step height and relative scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「階高與相對尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Step height and relative scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：criticalDepth=1.2 m; stepHeight=0.6 m; relativeDepth=1.2/0.6=2 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: criticalDepth=1.2 m; stepHeight=0.6 m; relativeDepth=1.2/0.6=2 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在連續變流量試驗中記錄水舌是否撞擊階面及流態轉換。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record nappe impact and regime transitions during a continuous discharge sweep.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：criticalDepth=1.2 m; stepHeight=0.6 m; relativeDepth=1.2/0.6=2 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: criticalDepth=1.2 m; stepHeight=0.6 m; relativeDepth=1.2/0.6=2 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「階高與相對尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Step height and relative scale\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：criticalDepth=1.2 m; stepHeight=0.6 m; relativeDepth=1.2/0.6=2 dimensionless。","表面變白就保證底部已獲充分含氣保護","表壓可直接與絕對蒸氣壓相減"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: criticalDepth=1.2 m; stepHeight=0.6 m; relativeDepth=1.2/0.6=2 dimensionless.","A white surface guarantees adequate air protection at the bed","Gauge pressure can be subtracted directly from absolute vapor pressure"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：criticalDepth=1.2 m; stepHeight=0.6 m; relativeDepth=1.2/0.6=2 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: criticalDepth=1.2 m; stepHeight=0.6 m; relativeDepth=1.2/0.6=2 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b246-v15-07","title":"階高與相對尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Step height and relative scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「階高與相對尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Step height and relative scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在連續變流量試驗中記錄水舌是否撞擊階面及流態轉換。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只測單一流量會漏掉過渡流態的不規則噴濺」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record nappe impact and regime transitions during a continuous discharge sweep. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Testing one discharge can miss irregular splashing in transitional flow. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以在連續變流量試驗中記錄水舌是否撞擊階面及流態轉換作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只測單一流量會漏掉過渡流態的不規則噴濺，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Record nappe impact and regime transitions during a continuous discharge sweep. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Testing one discharge can miss irregular splashing in transitional flow. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：只測單一流量會漏掉過渡流態的不規則噴濺。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Testing one discharge can miss irregular splashing in transitional flow. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在連續變流量試驗中記錄水舌是否撞擊階面及流態轉換。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只測單一流量會漏掉過渡流態的不規則噴濺」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Record nappe impact and regime transitions during a continuous discharge sweep. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Testing one discharge can miss irregular splashing in transitional flow. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以在連續變流量試驗中記錄水舌是否撞擊階面及流態轉換作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只測單一流量會漏掉過渡流態的不規則噴濺，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Record nappe impact and regime transitions during a continuous discharge sweep. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Testing one discharge can miss irregular splashing in transitional flow. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「階高與相對尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Step height and relative scale\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在連續變流量試驗中記錄水舌是否撞擊階面及流態轉換。","階梯表面耗能良好就代表底板不會受揚壓"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Record nappe impact and regime transitions during a continuous discharge sweep.","Effective surface dissipation means slabs cannot experience uplift"],"answer":1,"explanation":"在連續變流量試驗中記錄水舌是否撞擊階面及流態轉換。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record nappe impact and regime transitions during a continuous discharge sweep. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b246-v15-08","title":"階高與相對尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Step height and relative scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「階高與相對尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Step height and relative scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只測單一流量會漏掉過渡流態的不規則噴濺。診斷時應採取以下查核：在連續變流量試驗中記錄水舌是否撞擊階面及流態轉換，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Testing one discharge can miss irregular splashing in transitional flow. Diagnose it by the following check: Record nappe impact and regime transitions during a continuous discharge sweep. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「同一水深階高比保證所有坡度流態相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The same relative depth guarantees the same regime on every slope\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只測單一流量會漏掉過渡流態的不規則噴濺。診斷時應採取以下查核：在連續變流量試驗中記錄水舌是否撞擊階面及流態轉換，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Testing one discharge can miss irregular splashing in transitional flow. Diagnose it by the following check: Record nappe impact and regime transitions during a continuous discharge sweep. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「階高與相對尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Step height and relative scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","平均坡度正確就不必檢查個別階梯","只測單一流量會漏掉過渡流態的不規則噴濺。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Correct average slope removes the need to inspect individual steps","Testing one discharge can miss irregular splashing in transitional flow."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只測單一流量會漏掉過渡流態的不規則噴濺。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Testing one discharge can miss irregular splashing in transitional flow. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b246-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「階梯坡度與建造」與「階穴剪切與耗能」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Step geometry and construction\" and \"Cavity shear and dissipation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b246-v15-09","title":"階梯坡度與建造：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Step geometry and construction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「階梯坡度與建造」如何影響階梯式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Step geometry and construction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stepped spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"階梯由水平踏面與垂直階面組成，整體坡角影響重力沿坡分量、回流穴與施工模板。幾何閉合需核對總落差與總水平長度；局部突出或階尖錯台可能破壞原本流場，不能只驗收平均坡度而忽略局部平整性。 驗證時應逐階測量高程與踏面長度並與整體坡線閉合，並辨識以下失效情境：局部突出階尖可能增加低壓與磨耗集中。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「階梯坡度與建造」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Horizontal treads and vertical risers define the overall slope, influencing gravity components and recirculation cavities. Check total rise and horizontal run together. Local protrusions or displaced edges disturb the intended flow field, so average slope acceptance does not replace local surface and alignment surveys. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Survey every riser and tread and close them against the overall slope line. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: A projecting step edge can concentrate low pressure and abrasion. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Step geometry and construction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：stepRise=0.5 m; stepRun=1.0 m; slopeAngle=atan(0.5/1.0)=26.5651 degrees。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: stepRise=0.5 m; stepRun=1.0 m; slopeAngle=atan(0.5/1.0)=26.5651 degrees.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均坡度正確就不必檢查個別階梯」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Correct average slope removes the need to inspect individual steps\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「階梯坡度與建造」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Step geometry and construction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-09-k1","title":"階梯坡度與建造","titleEn":"Step geometry and construction","text":"階梯由水平踏面與垂直階面組成，整體坡角影響重力沿坡分量、回流穴與施工模板。幾何閉合需核對總落差與總水平長度；局部突出或階尖錯台可能破壞原本流場，不能只驗收平均坡度而忽略局部平整性。","textEn":"Horizontal treads and vertical risers define the overall slope, influencing gravity components and recirculation cavities. Check total rise and horizontal run together.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均坡度正確就不必檢查個別階梯 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Correct average slope removes the need to inspect individual steps Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「階梯坡度與建造」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Step geometry and construction\" is correct?","options":["階梯由水平踏面與垂直階面組成，整體坡角影響重力沿坡分量、回流穴與施工模板。","平均坡度正確就不必檢查個別階梯","只要增加階數總耗能就能無限制線性增加"],"optionsEn":["Horizontal treads and vertical risers define the overall slope, influencing gravity components and recirculation cavities.","Correct average slope removes the need to inspect individual steps","Adding steps increases total dissipation linearly without limit"],"answer":0,"explanation":"階梯由水平踏面與垂直階面組成，整體坡角影響重力沿坡分量、回流穴與施工模板。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Horizontal treads and vertical risers define the overall slope, influencing gravity components and recirculation cavities. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b246-v15-10","title":"階梯坡度與建造：定量估算","titleEn":"Step geometry and construction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「階梯坡度與建造」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Step geometry and construction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：stepRise=0.5 m; stepRun=1.0 m; slopeAngle=atan(0.5/1.0)=26.5651 degrees。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: stepRise=0.5 m; stepRun=1.0 m; slopeAngle=atan(0.5/1.0)=26.5651 degrees. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐階測量高程與踏面長度並與整體坡線閉合。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Survey every riser and tread and close them against the overall slope line.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：stepRise=0.5 m; stepRun=1.0 m; slopeAngle=atan(0.5/1.0)=26.5651 degrees。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: stepRise=0.5 m; stepRun=1.0 m; slopeAngle=atan(0.5/1.0)=26.5651 degrees. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「階梯坡度與建造」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Step geometry and construction\", which statement holds?","options":["混合層厚度與清水等效深度永遠相同","原創教學假設：stepRise=0.5 m; stepRun=1.0 m; slopeAngle=atan(0.5/1.0)=26.5651 degrees。","有階梯溢洪道就一定不需要末端消能"],"optionsEn":["Mixture thickness always equals clear-water equivalent depth","Original teaching assumptions: stepRise=0.5 m; stepRun=1.0 m; slopeAngle=atan(0.5/1.0)=26.5651 degrees.","Every stepped spillway eliminates the need for terminal dissipation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：stepRise=0.5 m; stepRun=1.0 m; slopeAngle=atan(0.5/1.0)=26.5651 degrees。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: stepRise=0.5 m; stepRun=1.0 m; slopeAngle=atan(0.5/1.0)=26.5651 degrees. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b246-v15-11","title":"階梯坡度與建造：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Step geometry and construction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「階梯坡度與建造」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Step geometry and construction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐階測量高程與踏面長度並與整體坡線閉合。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「局部突出階尖可能增加低壓與磨耗集中」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Survey every riser and tread and close them against the overall slope line. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A projecting step edge can concentrate low pressure and abrasion. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以逐階測量高程與踏面長度並與整體坡線閉合作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對局部突出階尖可能增加低壓與磨耗集中，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Survey every riser and tread and close them against the overall slope line. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A projecting step edge can concentrate low pressure and abrasion. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：局部突出階尖可能增加低壓與磨耗集中。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A projecting step edge can concentrate low pressure and abrasion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐階測量高程與踏面長度並與整體坡線閉合。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「局部突出階尖可能增加低壓與磨耗集中」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Survey every riser and tread and close them against the overall slope line. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A projecting step edge can concentrate low pressure and abrasion. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以逐階測量高程與踏面長度並與整體坡線閉合作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對局部突出階尖可能增加低壓與磨耗集中，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Survey every riser and tread and close them against the overall slope line. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A projecting step edge can concentrate low pressure and abrasion. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「階梯坡度與建造」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Step geometry and construction\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","相同福祿數也保證雷諾數自動相同","逐階測量高程與踏面長度並與整體坡線閉合。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Equal Froude numbers also guarantee equal Reynolds numbers","Survey every riser and tread and close them against the overall slope line."],"answer":2,"explanation":"逐階測量高程與踏面長度並與整體坡線閉合。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Survey every riser and tread and close them against the overall slope line. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b246-v15-12","title":"階梯坡度與建造：失效診斷","titleEn":"Step geometry and construction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「階梯坡度與建造」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Step geometry and construction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"局部突出階尖可能增加低壓與磨耗集中。診斷時應採取以下查核：逐階測量高程與踏面長度並與整體坡線閉合，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A projecting step edge can concentrate low pressure and abrasion. Diagnose it by the following check: Survey every riser and tread and close them against the overall slope line. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均坡度正確就不必檢查個別階梯」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Correct average slope removes the need to inspect individual steps\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"局部突出階尖可能增加低壓與磨耗集中。診斷時應採取以下查核：逐階測量高程與踏面長度並與整體坡線閉合，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"A projecting step edge can concentrate low pressure and abrasion. Diagnose it by the following check: Survey every riser and tread and close them against the overall slope line. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「階梯坡度與建造」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Step geometry and construction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["局部突出階尖可能增加低壓與磨耗集中。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只要增加階數總耗能就能無限制線性增加"],"optionsEn":["A projecting step edge can concentrate low pressure and abrasion.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Adding steps increases total dissipation linearly without limit"],"answer":0,"explanation":"局部突出階尖可能增加低壓與磨耗集中。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A projecting step edge can concentrate low pressure and abrasion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b246-v15-13","title":"階穴剪切與耗能：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cavity shear and dissipation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「階穴剪切與耗能」如何影響階梯式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cavity shear and dissipation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stepped spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"掠流在階尖連線上形成高速主流，階穴內回流透過剪切交換動量與能量。給定平均剪應力乘界面面積及相對速度可估交換功率，但不是完整耗能模型；相對速度與應力需由試驗取得，不能憑階數直接累加能量損失。 驗證時應比較階穴速度場與界面剪應力並檢查沿程剩餘比能，並辨識以下失效情境：把每階耗能當固定常數會忽略沿程流態演變。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「階穴剪切與耗能」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Skimming flow passes over step tips while cavity recirculation exchanges momentum through shear. Prescribed mean shear stress, interface area and relative velocity estimate transfer power, not a complete dissipation law. Obtain those quantities experimentally rather than assigning an identical energy loss to every step. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare cavity velocities and interface shear with residual specific energy downstream. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Assigning constant dissipation to every step ignores evolving flow conditions. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cavity shear and dissipation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：meanShear=400 Pa; interfaceArea=3 m2; relativeVelocity=5 m/s; transferPower=400*3*5/1000=6 kW。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: meanShear=400 Pa; interfaceArea=3 m2; relativeVelocity=5 m/s; transferPower=400*3*5/1000=6 kW.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要增加階數總耗能就能無限制線性增加」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding steps increases total dissipation linearly without limit\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「階穴剪切與耗能」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cavity shear and dissipation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-13-k1","title":"階穴剪切與耗能","titleEn":"Cavity shear and dissipation","text":"掠流在階尖連線上形成高速主流，階穴內回流透過剪切交換動量與能量。給定平均剪應力乘界面面積及相對速度可估交換功率，但不是完整耗能模型；相對速度與應力需由試驗取得，不能憑階數直接累加能量損失。","textEn":"Skimming flow passes over step tips while cavity recirculation exchanges momentum through shear. Prescribed mean shear stress, interface area and relative velocity estimate transfer power, not a complete dissipation law.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要增加階數總耗能就能無限制線性增加 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding steps increases total dissipation linearly without limit Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「階穴剪切與耗能」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cavity shear and dissipation\" is correct?","options":["只要增加階數總耗能就能無限制線性增加","掠流在階尖連線上形成高速主流，階穴內回流透過剪切交換動量與能量。","表面變白就保證底部已獲充分含氣保護"],"optionsEn":["Adding steps increases total dissipation linearly without limit","Skimming flow passes over step tips while cavity recirculation exchanges momentum through shear.","A white surface guarantees adequate air protection at the bed"],"answer":1,"explanation":"掠流在階尖連線上形成高速主流，階穴內回流透過剪切交換動量與能量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Skimming flow passes over step tips while cavity recirculation exchanges momentum through shear. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b246-v15-14","title":"階穴剪切與耗能：定量估算","titleEn":"Cavity shear and dissipation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「階穴剪切與耗能」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cavity shear and dissipation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：meanShear=400 Pa; interfaceArea=3 m2; relativeVelocity=5 m/s; transferPower=400*3*5/1000=6 kW。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: meanShear=400 Pa; interfaceArea=3 m2; relativeVelocity=5 m/s; transferPower=400*3*5/1000=6 kW. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較階穴速度場與界面剪應力並檢查沿程剩餘比能。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare cavity velocities and interface shear with residual specific energy downstream.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：meanShear=400 Pa; interfaceArea=3 m2; relativeVelocity=5 m/s; transferPower=400*3*5/1000=6 kW。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: meanShear=400 Pa; interfaceArea=3 m2; relativeVelocity=5 m/s; transferPower=400*3*5/1000=6 kW. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「階穴剪切與耗能」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cavity shear and dissipation\", which statement holds?","options":["表壓可直接與絕對蒸氣壓相減","階梯表面耗能良好就代表底板不會受揚壓","原創教學假設：meanShear=400 Pa; interfaceArea=3 m2; relativeVelocity=5 m/s; transferPower=400*3*5/1000=6 kW。"],"optionsEn":["Gauge pressure can be subtracted directly from absolute vapor pressure","Effective surface dissipation means slabs cannot experience uplift","Original teaching assumptions: meanShear=400 Pa; interfaceArea=3 m2; relativeVelocity=5 m/s; transferPower=400*3*5/1000=6 kW."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：meanShear=400 Pa; interfaceArea=3 m2; relativeVelocity=5 m/s; transferPower=400*3*5/1000=6 kW。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: meanShear=400 Pa; interfaceArea=3 m2; relativeVelocity=5 m/s; transferPower=400*3*5/1000=6 kW. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b246-v15-15","title":"階穴剪切與耗能：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cavity shear and dissipation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「階穴剪切與耗能」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cavity shear and dissipation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較階穴速度場與界面剪應力並檢查沿程剩餘比能。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把每階耗能當固定常數會忽略沿程流態演變」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare cavity velocities and interface shear with residual specific energy downstream. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Assigning constant dissipation to every step ignores evolving flow conditions. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以比較階穴速度場與界面剪應力並檢查沿程剩餘比能作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把每階耗能當固定常數會忽略沿程流態演變，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare cavity velocities and interface shear with residual specific energy downstream. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Assigning constant dissipation to every step ignores evolving flow conditions. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：把每階耗能當固定常數會忽略沿程流態演變。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Assigning constant dissipation to every step ignores evolving flow conditions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較階穴速度場與界面剪應力並檢查沿程剩餘比能。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把每階耗能當固定常數會忽略沿程流態演變」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare cavity velocities and interface shear with residual specific energy downstream. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Assigning constant dissipation to every step ignores evolving flow conditions. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以比較階穴速度場與界面剪應力並檢查沿程剩餘比能作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把每階耗能當固定常數會忽略沿程流態演變，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare cavity velocities and interface shear with residual specific energy downstream. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Assigning constant dissipation to every step ignores evolving flow conditions. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「階穴剪切與耗能」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cavity shear and dissipation\"?","options":["比較階穴速度場與界面剪應力並檢查沿程剩餘比能。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","臨界水深就是每一階上的實際水深"],"optionsEn":["Compare cavity velocities and interface shear with residual specific energy downstream.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Critical depth equals actual flow depth on every step"],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較階穴速度場與界面剪應力並檢查沿程剩餘比能。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare cavity velocities and interface shear with residual specific energy downstream. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b246-v15-16","title":"階穴剪切與耗能：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cavity shear and dissipation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「階穴剪切與耗能」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cavity shear and dissipation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把每階耗能當固定常數會忽略沿程流態演變。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較階穴速度場與界面剪應力並檢查沿程剩餘比能，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Assigning constant dissipation to every step ignores evolving flow conditions. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare cavity velocities and interface shear with residual specific energy downstream. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要增加階數總耗能就能無限制線性增加」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding steps increases total dissipation linearly without limit\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把每階耗能當固定常數會忽略沿程流態演變。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較階穴速度場與界面剪應力並檢查沿程剩餘比能，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Assigning constant dissipation to every step ignores evolving flow conditions. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare cavity velocities and interface shear with residual specific energy downstream. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「階穴剪切與耗能」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cavity shear and dissipation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把每階耗能當固定常數會忽略沿程流態演變。","表面變白就保證底部已獲充分含氣保護"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Assigning constant dissipation to every step ignores evolving flow conditions.","A white surface guarantees adequate air protection at the bed"],"answer":1,"explanation":"把每階耗能當固定常數會忽略沿程流態演變。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Assigning constant dissipation to every step ignores evolving flow conditions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b246-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「自含氣起點判讀」與「混合水深與牆高」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Self-aeration inception identification\" and \"Mixture depth and wall height\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b246-v15-17","title":"自含氣起點判讀：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Self-aeration inception identification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「自含氣起點判讀」如何影響階梯式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Self-aeration inception identification” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stepped spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"湍流邊界層向自由水面發展後可開始大量捲氣，起點之前的近壁清水區可能更易受氣蝕影響。以觀測座標描述起點位置並不預測其隨流量變化；應結合壓力、含氣與邊界層量測，不能只看表面是否呈白色。 驗證時應沿槽測量近壁含氣率並將其與表面白化起點比較，並辨識以下失效情境：表面含氣但近壁仍清水可能留下局部氣蝕風險。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「自含氣起點判讀」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Air entrainment develops when turbulence reaches the free surface, leaving an upstream clear-water region potentially more vulnerable to cavitation. An observed inception coordinate does not predict its discharge dependence. Combine pressure, concentration and boundary-layer measurements rather than relying on a white surface appearance alone. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure near-wall air concentration along the chute and compare surface whitening onset. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: An aerated surface with clear water near the wall leaves local cavitation risk. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Self-aeration inception identification” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Measured inceptionDistance=18 m; totalChuteLength=60 m; clearRegionFraction=18/60=0.30 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Measured inceptionDistance=18 m; totalChuteLength=60 m; clearRegionFraction=18/60=0.30 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「表面變白就保證底部已獲充分含氣保護」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A white surface guarantees adequate air protection at the bed\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「自含氣起點判讀」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Self-aeration inception identification”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-17-k1","title":"自含氣起點判讀","titleEn":"Self-aeration inception identification","text":"湍流邊界層向自由水面發展後可開始大量捲氣，起點之前的近壁清水區可能更易受氣蝕影響。以觀測座標描述起點位置並不預測其隨流量變化；應結合壓力、含氣與邊界層量測，不能只看表面是否呈白色。","textEn":"Air entrainment develops when turbulence reaches the free surface, leaving an upstream clear-water region potentially more vulnerable to cavitation. An observed inception coordinate does not predict its discharge dependence.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：表面變白就保證底部已獲充分含氣保護 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A white surface guarantees adequate air protection at the bed Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「自含氣起點判讀」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Self-aeration inception identification\" is correct?","options":["表面變白就保證底部已獲充分含氣保護","混合層厚度與清水等效深度永遠相同","湍流邊界層向自由水面發展後可開始大量捲氣，起點之前的近壁清水區可能更易受氣蝕影響。"],"optionsEn":["A white surface guarantees adequate air protection at the bed","Mixture thickness always equals clear-water equivalent depth","Air entrainment develops when turbulence reaches the free surface, leaving an upstream clear-water region potentially more vulnerable to cavitation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"湍流邊界層向自由水面發展後可開始大量捲氣，起點之前的近壁清水區可能更易受氣蝕影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Air entrainment develops when turbulence reaches the free surface, leaving an upstream clear-water region potentially more vulnerable to cavitation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b246-v15-18","title":"自含氣起點判讀：定量估算","titleEn":"Self-aeration inception identification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「自含氣起點判讀」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Self-aeration inception identification” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Measured inceptionDistance=18 m; totalChuteLength=60 m; clearRegionFraction=18/60=0.30 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Measured inceptionDistance=18 m; totalChuteLength=60 m; clearRegionFraction=18/60=0.30 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿槽測量近壁含氣率並將其與表面白化起點比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure near-wall air concentration along the chute and compare surface whitening onset.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Measured inceptionDistance=18 m; totalChuteLength=60 m; clearRegionFraction=18/60=0.30 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Measured inceptionDistance=18 m; totalChuteLength=60 m; clearRegionFraction=18/60=0.30 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「自含氣起點判讀」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Self-aeration inception identification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：Measured inceptionDistance=18 m; totalChuteLength=60 m; clearRegionFraction=18/60=0.30 dimensionless。","有階梯溢洪道就一定不需要末端消能","相同福祿數也保證雷諾數自動相同"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Measured inceptionDistance=18 m; totalChuteLength=60 m; clearRegionFraction=18/60=0.30 dimensionless.","Every stepped spillway eliminates the need for terminal dissipation","Equal Froude numbers also guarantee equal Reynolds numbers"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Measured inceptionDistance=18 m; totalChuteLength=60 m; clearRegionFraction=18/60=0.30 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Measured inceptionDistance=18 m; totalChuteLength=60 m; clearRegionFraction=18/60=0.30 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b246-v15-19","title":"自含氣起點判讀：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Self-aeration inception identification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「自含氣起點判讀」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Self-aeration inception identification” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿槽測量近壁含氣率並將其與表面白化起點比較。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「表面含氣但近壁仍清水可能留下局部氣蝕風險」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure near-wall air concentration along the chute and compare surface whitening onset. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: An aerated surface with clear water near the wall leaves local cavitation risk. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以沿槽測量近壁含氣率並將其與表面白化起點比較作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對表面含氣但近壁仍清水可能留下局部氣蝕風險，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure near-wall air concentration along the chute and compare surface whitening onset. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: An aerated surface with clear water near the wall leaves local cavitation risk. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：表面含氣但近壁仍清水可能留下局部氣蝕風險。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An aerated surface with clear water near the wall leaves local cavitation risk. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿槽測量近壁含氣率並將其與表面白化起點比較。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「表面含氣但近壁仍清水可能留下局部氣蝕風險」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure near-wall air concentration along the chute and compare surface whitening onset. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: An aerated surface with clear water near the wall leaves local cavitation risk. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以沿槽測量近壁含氣率並將其與表面白化起點比較作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對表面含氣但近壁仍清水可能留下局部氣蝕風險，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure near-wall air concentration along the chute and compare surface whitening onset. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: An aerated surface with clear water near the wall leaves local cavitation risk. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「自含氣起點判讀」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Self-aeration inception identification\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","沿槽測量近壁含氣率並將其與表面白化起點比較。","同一水深階高比保證所有坡度流態相同"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure near-wall air concentration along the chute and compare surface whitening onset.","The same relative depth guarantees the same regime on every slope"],"answer":1,"explanation":"沿槽測量近壁含氣率並將其與表面白化起點比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure near-wall air concentration along the chute and compare surface whitening onset. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b246-v15-20","title":"自含氣起點判讀：失效診斷","titleEn":"Self-aeration inception identification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「自含氣起點判讀」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Self-aeration inception identification” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"表面含氣但近壁仍清水可能留下局部氣蝕風險。診斷時應採取以下查核：沿槽測量近壁含氣率並將其與表面白化起點比較，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An aerated surface with clear water near the wall leaves local cavitation risk. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure near-wall air concentration along the chute and compare surface whitening onset. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「表面變白就保證底部已獲充分含氣保護」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A white surface guarantees adequate air protection at the bed\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"表面含氣但近壁仍清水可能留下局部氣蝕風險。診斷時應採取以下查核：沿槽測量近壁含氣率並將其與表面白化起點比較，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"An aerated surface with clear water near the wall leaves local cavitation risk. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure near-wall air concentration along the chute and compare surface whitening onset. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「自含氣起點判讀」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Self-aeration inception identification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","混合層厚度與清水等效深度永遠相同","表面含氣但近壁仍清水可能留下局部氣蝕風險。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Mixture thickness always equals clear-water equivalent depth","An aerated surface with clear water near the wall leaves local cavitation risk."],"answer":2,"explanation":"表面含氣但近壁仍清水可能留下局部氣蝕風險。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An aerated surface with clear water near the wall leaves local cavitation risk. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b246-v15-21","title":"混合水深與牆高：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Mixture depth and wall height: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「混合水深與牆高」如何影響階梯式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Mixture depth and wall height” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stepped spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"空氣加入後可使水氣混合層增厚，邊牆需求因此不能只看清水等效深度。均勻含氣率公式僅作截面平均估算，波峰、噴濺與橫向聚流還需額外檢查；牆高也涉及結構與排水，不可直接由一個含氣比決定。 驗證時應以含氣剖面積分核對等效水深並記錄波峰高度，並辨識以下失效情境：只用平均混合深度配置牆高會漏掉波峰越流。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「混合水深與牆高」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Entrained air thickens the mixture, so wall assessment cannot rely only on clear-water equivalent depth. A uniform-concentration relation estimates a sectional mean, while waves, splash and transverse convergence need additional checks. Wall height also involves structural and drainage requirements beyond one air-fraction calculation. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Integrate air profiles to check equivalent water depth and record wave crests. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Sizing walls to mean mixture depth alone overlooks wave overtopping. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Mixture depth and wall height” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：ClearWaterDepth=0.80 m; meanAirFraction=0.25; mixtureDepth=0.80/(1-0.25)=1.06667 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: ClearWaterDepth=0.80 m; meanAirFraction=0.25; mixtureDepth=0.80/(1-0.25)=1.06667 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「混合層厚度與清水等效深度永遠相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Mixture thickness always equals clear-water equivalent depth\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「混合水深與牆高」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Mixture depth and wall height”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-21-k1","title":"混合水深與牆高","titleEn":"Mixture depth and wall height","text":"空氣加入後可使水氣混合層增厚，邊牆需求因此不能只看清水等效深度。均勻含氣率公式僅作截面平均估算，波峰、噴濺與橫向聚流還需額外檢查；牆高也涉及結構與排水，不可直接由一個含氣比決定。","textEn":"Entrained air thickens the mixture, so wall assessment cannot rely only on clear-water equivalent depth. A uniform-concentration relation estimates a sectional mean, while waves, splash and transverse convergence need additional checks.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混合層厚度與清水等效深度永遠相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Mixture thickness always equals clear-water equivalent depth Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「混合水深與牆高」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Mixture depth and wall height\" is correct?","options":["空氣加入後可使水氣混合層增厚，邊牆需求因此不能只看清水等效深度。","混合層厚度與清水等效深度永遠相同","表壓可直接與絕對蒸氣壓相減"],"optionsEn":["Entrained air thickens the mixture, so wall assessment cannot rely only on clear-water equivalent depth.","Mixture thickness always equals clear-water equivalent depth","Gauge pressure can be subtracted directly from absolute vapor pressure"],"answer":0,"explanation":"空氣加入後可使水氣混合層增厚，邊牆需求因此不能只看清水等效深度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Entrained air thickens the mixture, so wall assessment cannot rely only on clear-water equivalent depth. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b246-v15-22","title":"混合水深與牆高：定量估算","titleEn":"Mixture depth and wall height: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「混合水深與牆高」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Mixture depth and wall height” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：ClearWaterDepth=0.80 m; meanAirFraction=0.25; mixtureDepth=0.80/(1-0.25)=1.06667 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: ClearWaterDepth=0.80 m; meanAirFraction=0.25; mixtureDepth=0.80/(1-0.25)=1.06667 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以含氣剖面積分核對等效水深並記錄波峰高度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Integrate air profiles to check equivalent water depth and record wave crests.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：ClearWaterDepth=0.80 m; meanAirFraction=0.25; mixtureDepth=0.80/(1-0.25)=1.06667 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: ClearWaterDepth=0.80 m; meanAirFraction=0.25; mixtureDepth=0.80/(1-0.25)=1.06667 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「混合水深與牆高」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Mixture depth and wall height\", which statement holds?","options":["階梯表面耗能良好就代表底板不會受揚壓","原創教學假設：ClearWaterDepth=0.80 m; meanAirFraction=0.25; mixtureDepth=0.80/(1-0.25)=1.06667 m。","臨界水深就是每一階上的實際水深"],"optionsEn":["Effective surface dissipation means slabs cannot experience uplift","Original teaching assumptions: ClearWaterDepth=0.80 m; meanAirFraction=0.25; mixtureDepth=0.80/(1-0.25)=1.06667 m.","Critical depth equals actual flow depth on every step"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：ClearWaterDepth=0.80 m; meanAirFraction=0.25; mixtureDepth=0.80/(1-0.25)=1.06667 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: ClearWaterDepth=0.80 m; meanAirFraction=0.25; mixtureDepth=0.80/(1-0.25)=1.06667 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b246-v15-23","title":"混合水深與牆高：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Mixture depth and wall height: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「混合水深與牆高」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Mixture depth and wall height” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以含氣剖面積分核對等效水深並記錄波峰高度。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只用平均混合深度配置牆高會漏掉波峰越流」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Integrate air profiles to check equivalent water depth and record wave crests. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Sizing walls to mean mixture depth alone overlooks wave overtopping. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以含氣剖面積分核對等效水深並記錄波峰高度作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只用平均混合深度配置牆高會漏掉波峰越流，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Integrate air profiles to check equivalent water depth and record wave crests. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Sizing walls to mean mixture depth alone overlooks wave overtopping. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：只用平均混合深度配置牆高會漏掉波峰越流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Sizing walls to mean mixture depth alone overlooks wave overtopping. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以含氣剖面積分核對等效水深並記錄波峰高度。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只用平均混合深度配置牆高會漏掉波峰越流」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Integrate air profiles to check equivalent water depth and record wave crests. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Sizing walls to mean mixture depth alone overlooks wave overtopping. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以含氣剖面積分核對等效水深並記錄波峰高度作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只用平均混合深度配置牆高會漏掉波峰越流，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Integrate air profiles to check equivalent water depth and record wave crests. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Sizing walls to mean mixture depth alone overlooks wave overtopping. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「混合水深與牆高」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Mixture depth and wall height\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","平均坡度正確就不必檢查個別階梯","以含氣剖面積分核對等效水深並記錄波峰高度。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Correct average slope removes the need to inspect individual steps","Integrate air profiles to check equivalent water depth and record wave crests."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以含氣剖面積分核對等效水深並記錄波峰高度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Integrate air profiles to check equivalent water depth and record wave crests. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b246-v15-24","title":"混合水深與牆高：失效診斷","titleEn":"Mixture depth and wall height: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「混合水深與牆高」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Mixture depth and wall height” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只用平均混合深度配置牆高會漏掉波峰越流。診斷時應採取以下查核：以含氣剖面積分核對等效水深並記錄波峰高度，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Sizing walls to mean mixture depth alone overlooks wave overtopping. Diagnose it by the following check: Integrate air profiles to check equivalent water depth and record wave crests. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混合層厚度與清水等效深度永遠相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Mixture thickness always equals clear-water equivalent depth\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只用平均混合深度配置牆高會漏掉波峰越流。診斷時應採取以下查核：以含氣剖面積分核對等效水深並記錄波峰高度，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Sizing walls to mean mixture depth alone overlooks wave overtopping. Diagnose it by the following check: Integrate air profiles to check equivalent water depth and record wave crests. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「混合水深與牆高」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Mixture depth and wall height\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只用平均混合深度配置牆高會漏掉波峰越流。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","表壓可直接與絕對蒸氣壓相減"],"optionsEn":["Sizing walls to mean mixture depth alone overlooks wave overtopping.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Gauge pressure can be subtracted directly from absolute vapor pressure"],"answer":0,"explanation":"只用平均混合深度配置牆高會漏掉波峰越流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Sizing walls to mean mixture depth alone overlooks wave overtopping. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b246-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「近壁低壓與氣蝕」與「下游剩餘能量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Near-wall pressure and cavitation\" and \"Downstream residual energy\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b246-v15-25","title":"近壁低壓與氣蝕：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Near-wall pressure and cavitation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「近壁低壓與氣蝕」如何影響階梯式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Near-wall pressure and cavitation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stepped spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"階尖後方流動分離可產生低壓，局部壓力與蒸氣壓的距離比表面含氣外觀更直接。氣蝕指標需用一致的絕對壓力與參考速度；同一指標下表面缺陷與氣核不同仍會改變起始，因此需對實際階面品質驗證。 驗證時應同步量測階尖後低壓與近壁含氣率並記錄表面缺陷，並辨識以下失效情境：把表壓直接代入會錯估距蒸氣壓的餘量。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「近壁低壓與氣蝕」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separation behind step edges creates low pressure. Compare local absolute pressure with vapor pressure using a consistent velocity reference. Surface defects and nuclei affect inception even at similar indices; visible aeration does not replace verification of wall conditions and actual near-wall protection. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure downstream-edge pressure and near-wall air together and document surface defects. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Inserting gauge pressure directly misstates the margin above vapor pressure. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Near-wall pressure and cavitation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：pAbsolute=80 kPa; vaporPressure=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=18 m/s; sigma=(80000-2300)/(0.5*1000*18**2)=0.479630。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: pAbsolute=80 kPa; vaporPressure=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=18 m/s; sigma=(80000-2300)/(0.5*1000*18**2)=0.479630.","failure":"常見誤解：「表壓可直接與絕對蒸氣壓相減」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Gauge pressure can be subtracted directly from absolute vapor pressure\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「近壁低壓與氣蝕」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Near-wall pressure and cavitation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-25-k1","title":"近壁低壓與氣蝕","titleEn":"Near-wall pressure and cavitation","text":"階尖後方流動分離可產生低壓，局部壓力與蒸氣壓的距離比表面含氣外觀更直接。氣蝕指標需用一致的絕對壓力與參考速度；同一指標下表面缺陷與氣核不同仍會改變起始，因此需對實際階面品質驗證。","textEn":"Separation behind step edges creates low pressure. Compare local absolute pressure with vapor pressure using a consistent velocity reference.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：表壓可直接與絕對蒸氣壓相減 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Gauge pressure can be subtracted directly from absolute vapor pressure Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「近壁低壓與氣蝕」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Near-wall pressure and cavitation\" is correct?","options":["表壓可直接與絕對蒸氣壓相減","階尖後方流動分離可產生低壓，局部壓力與蒸氣壓的距離比表面含氣外觀更直接。","有階梯溢洪道就一定不需要末端消能"],"optionsEn":["Gauge pressure can be subtracted directly from absolute vapor pressure","Separation behind step edges creates low pressure.","Every stepped spillway eliminates the need for terminal dissipation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"階尖後方流動分離可產生低壓，局部壓力與蒸氣壓的距離比表面含氣外觀更直接。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separation behind step edges creates low pressure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b246-v15-26","title":"近壁低壓與氣蝕：定量估算","titleEn":"Near-wall pressure and cavitation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「近壁低壓與氣蝕」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Near-wall pressure and cavitation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：pAbsolute=80 kPa; vaporPressure=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=18 m/s; sigma=(80000-2300)/(0.5*1000*18**2)=0.479630。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: pAbsolute=80 kPa; vaporPressure=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=18 m/s; sigma=(80000-2300)/(0.5*1000*18**2)=0.479630. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測階尖後低壓與近壁含氣率並記錄表面缺陷。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure downstream-edge pressure and near-wall air together and document surface defects.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：pAbsolute=80 kPa; vaporPressure=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=18 m/s; sigma=(80000-2300)/(0.5*1000*18**2)=0.479630。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pAbsolute=80 kPa; vaporPressure=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=18 m/s; sigma=(80000-2300)/(0.5*1000*18**2)=0.479630. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「近壁低壓與氣蝕」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Near-wall pressure and cavitation\", which statement holds?","options":["相同福祿數也保證雷諾數自動相同","同一水深階高比保證所有坡度流態相同","原創教學假設：pAbsolute=80 kPa; vaporPressure=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=18 m/s; sigma=(80000-2300)/(0.5*1000*18**2)=0.479630。"],"optionsEn":["Equal Froude numbers also guarantee equal Reynolds numbers","The same relative depth guarantees the same regime on every slope","Original teaching assumptions: pAbsolute=80 kPa; vaporPressure=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=18 m/s; sigma=(80000-2300)/(0.5*1000*18**2)=0.479630."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：pAbsolute=80 kPa; vaporPressure=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=18 m/s; sigma=(80000-2300)/(0.5*1000*18**2)=0.479630。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pAbsolute=80 kPa; vaporPressure=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=18 m/s; sigma=(80000-2300)/(0.5*1000*18**2)=0.479630. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b246-v15-27","title":"近壁低壓與氣蝕：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Near-wall pressure and cavitation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「近壁低壓與氣蝕」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Near-wall pressure and cavitation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測階尖後低壓與近壁含氣率並記錄表面缺陷。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把表壓直接代入會錯估距蒸氣壓的餘量」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure downstream-edge pressure and near-wall air together and document surface defects. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Inserting gauge pressure directly misstates the margin above vapor pressure. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以同步量測階尖後低壓與近壁含氣率並記錄表面缺陷作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把表壓直接代入會錯估距蒸氣壓的餘量，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure downstream-edge pressure and near-wall air together and document surface defects. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Inserting gauge pressure directly misstates the margin above vapor pressure. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：把表壓直接代入會錯估距蒸氣壓的餘量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Inserting gauge pressure directly misstates the margin above vapor pressure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測階尖後低壓與近壁含氣率並記錄表面缺陷。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把表壓直接代入會錯估距蒸氣壓的餘量」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure downstream-edge pressure and near-wall air together and document surface defects. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Inserting gauge pressure directly misstates the margin above vapor pressure. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以同步量測階尖後低壓與近壁含氣率並記錄表面缺陷作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把表壓直接代入會錯估距蒸氣壓的餘量，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure downstream-edge pressure and near-wall air together and document surface defects. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Inserting gauge pressure directly misstates the margin above vapor pressure. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「近壁低壓與氣蝕」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Near-wall pressure and cavitation\"?","options":["同步量測階尖後低壓與近壁含氣率並記錄表面缺陷。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要增加階數總耗能就能無限制線性增加"],"optionsEn":["Measure downstream-edge pressure and near-wall air together and document surface defects.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Adding steps increases total dissipation linearly without limit"],"answer":0,"explanation":"同步量測階尖後低壓與近壁含氣率並記錄表面缺陷。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure downstream-edge pressure and near-wall air together and document surface defects. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b246-v15-28","title":"近壁低壓與氣蝕：失效診斷","titleEn":"Near-wall pressure and cavitation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「近壁低壓與氣蝕」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Near-wall pressure and cavitation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把表壓直接代入會錯估距蒸氣壓的餘量。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步量測階尖後低壓與近壁含氣率並記錄表面缺陷，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Inserting gauge pressure directly misstates the margin above vapor pressure. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure downstream-edge pressure and near-wall air together and document surface defects. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「表壓可直接與絕對蒸氣壓相減」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Gauge pressure can be subtracted directly from absolute vapor pressure\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把表壓直接代入會錯估距蒸氣壓的餘量。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步量測階尖後低壓與近壁含氣率並記錄表面缺陷，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Inserting gauge pressure directly misstates the margin above vapor pressure. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure downstream-edge pressure and near-wall air together and document surface defects. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「近壁低壓與氣蝕」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Near-wall pressure and cavitation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把表壓直接代入會錯估距蒸氣壓的餘量。","有階梯溢洪道就一定不需要末端消能"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Inserting gauge pressure directly misstates the margin above vapor pressure.","Every stepped spillway eliminates the need for terminal dissipation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"把表壓直接代入會錯估距蒸氣壓的餘量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Inserting gauge pressure directly misstates the margin above vapor pressure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b246-v15-29","title":"下游剩餘能量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Downstream residual energy: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「下游剩餘能量」如何影響階梯式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Downstream residual energy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stepped spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"階梯可在陡槽沿程耗能，但下游仍有速度水頭與水深所含比能，需要與尾水和消能池配合。以矩形清水等效斷面估比能時應明示速度分布修正假設；不應因階梯表面看似激烈翻滾就宣稱可以省去末端消能。 驗證時應比較槽末清水等效比能與消能池入流工況表，並辨識以下失效情境：忽略剩餘速度水頭會低估下游沖刷需求。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「下游剩餘能量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Steps dissipate energy along the chute, yet depth and velocity head remain at its end. Coordinate that residual energy with tailwater and terminal dissipation. A rectangular clear-water equivalent section assumes a velocity-distribution correction; vigorous visible turbulence does not prove that a terminal basin is unnecessary. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare terminal clear-water equivalent energy with basin approach-condition tables. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Ignoring residual velocity head understates downstream scour demand. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Downstream residual energy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：depth=1.1 m; meanV=8 m/s; energyCoefficient=1; specificEnergy=1.1+8**2/(2*9.81)=4.36198 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: depth=1.1 m; meanV=8 m/s; energyCoefficient=1; specificEnergy=1.1+8**2/(2*9.81)=4.36198 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「有階梯溢洪道就一定不需要末端消能」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every stepped spillway eliminates the need for terminal dissipation\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「下游剩餘能量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Downstream residual energy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-29-k1","title":"下游剩餘能量","titleEn":"Downstream residual energy","text":"階梯可在陡槽沿程耗能，但下游仍有速度水頭與水深所含比能，需要與尾水和消能池配合。以矩形清水等效斷面估比能時應明示速度分布修正假設；不應因階梯表面看似激烈翻滾就宣稱可以省去末端消能。","textEn":"Steps dissipate energy along the chute, yet depth and velocity head remain at its end. Coordinate that residual energy with tailwater and terminal dissipation.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：有階梯溢洪道就一定不需要末端消能 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every stepped spillway eliminates the need for terminal dissipation Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「下游剩餘能量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Downstream residual energy\" is correct?","options":["有階梯溢洪道就一定不需要末端消能","階梯表面耗能良好就代表底板不會受揚壓","階梯可在陡槽沿程耗能，但下游仍有速度水頭與水深所含比能，需要與尾水和消能池配合。"],"optionsEn":["Every stepped spillway eliminates the need for terminal dissipation","Effective surface dissipation means slabs cannot experience uplift","Steps dissipate energy along the chute, yet depth and velocity head remain at its end."],"answer":2,"explanation":"階梯可在陡槽沿程耗能，但下游仍有速度水頭與水深所含比能，需要與尾水和消能池配合。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Steps dissipate energy along the chute, yet depth and velocity head remain at its end. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b246-v15-30","title":"下游剩餘能量：定量估算","titleEn":"Downstream residual energy: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「下游剩餘能量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Downstream residual energy” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：depth=1.1 m; meanV=8 m/s; energyCoefficient=1; specificEnergy=1.1+8**2/(2*9.81)=4.36198 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: depth=1.1 m; meanV=8 m/s; energyCoefficient=1; specificEnergy=1.1+8**2/(2*9.81)=4.36198 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較槽末清水等效比能與消能池入流工況表。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare terminal clear-water equivalent energy with basin approach-condition tables.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：depth=1.1 m; meanV=8 m/s; energyCoefficient=1; specificEnergy=1.1+8**2/(2*9.81)=4.36198 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: depth=1.1 m; meanV=8 m/s; energyCoefficient=1; specificEnergy=1.1+8**2/(2*9.81)=4.36198 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「下游剩餘能量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Downstream residual energy\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：depth=1.1 m; meanV=8 m/s; energyCoefficient=1; specificEnergy=1.1+8**2/(2*9.81)=4.36198 m。","臨界水深就是每一階上的實際水深","平均坡度正確就不必檢查個別階梯"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: depth=1.1 m; meanV=8 m/s; energyCoefficient=1; specificEnergy=1.1+8**2/(2*9.81)=4.36198 m.","Critical depth equals actual flow depth on every step","Correct average slope removes the need to inspect individual steps"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：depth=1.1 m; meanV=8 m/s; energyCoefficient=1; specificEnergy=1.1+8**2/(2*9.81)=4.36198 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: depth=1.1 m; meanV=8 m/s; energyCoefficient=1; specificEnergy=1.1+8**2/(2*9.81)=4.36198 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b246-v15-31","title":"下游剩餘能量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Downstream residual energy: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「下游剩餘能量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Downstream residual energy” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較槽末清水等效比能與消能池入流工況表。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「忽略剩餘速度水頭會低估下游沖刷需求」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare terminal clear-water equivalent energy with basin approach-condition tables. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Ignoring residual velocity head understates downstream scour demand. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以比較槽末清水等效比能與消能池入流工況表作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對忽略剩餘速度水頭會低估下游沖刷需求，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare terminal clear-water equivalent energy with basin approach-condition tables. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Ignoring residual velocity head understates downstream scour demand. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略剩餘速度水頭會低估下游沖刷需求。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring residual velocity head understates downstream scour demand. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較槽末清水等效比能與消能池入流工況表。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「忽略剩餘速度水頭會低估下游沖刷需求」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare terminal clear-water equivalent energy with basin approach-condition tables. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Ignoring residual velocity head understates downstream scour demand. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以比較槽末清水等效比能與消能池入流工況表作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對忽略剩餘速度水頭會低估下游沖刷需求，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare terminal clear-water equivalent energy with basin approach-condition tables. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Ignoring residual velocity head understates downstream scour demand. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「下游剩餘能量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Downstream residual energy\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比較槽末清水等效比能與消能池入流工況表。","表面變白就保證底部已獲充分含氣保護"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Compare terminal clear-water equivalent energy with basin approach-condition tables.","A white surface guarantees adequate air protection at the bed"],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較槽末清水等效比能與消能池入流工況表。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare terminal clear-water equivalent energy with basin approach-condition tables. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b246-v15-32","title":"下游剩餘能量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Downstream residual energy: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「下游剩餘能量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Downstream residual energy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略剩餘速度水頭會低估下游沖刷需求。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較槽末清水等效比能與消能池入流工況表，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring residual velocity head understates downstream scour demand. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare terminal clear-water equivalent energy with basin approach-condition tables. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「有階梯溢洪道就一定不需要末端消能」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every stepped spillway eliminates the need for terminal dissipation\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略剩餘速度水頭會低估下游沖刷需求。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較槽末清水等效比能與消能池入流工況表，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Ignoring residual velocity head understates downstream scour demand. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare terminal clear-water equivalent energy with basin approach-condition tables. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「下游剩餘能量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Downstream residual energy\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","階梯表面耗能良好就代表底板不會受揚壓","忽略剩餘速度水頭會低估下游沖刷需求。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Effective surface dissipation means slabs cannot experience uplift","Ignoring residual velocity head understates downstream scour demand."],"answer":2,"explanation":"忽略剩餘速度水頭會低估下游沖刷需求。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring residual velocity head understates downstream scour demand. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b246-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「接縫滲壓與穩定」與「縮尺黏性與可比性」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Joint pressure and slab stability\" and \"Scale viscosity and comparability\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b246-v15-33","title":"接縫滲壓與穩定：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Joint pressure and slab stability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「接縫滲壓與穩定」如何影響階梯式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Joint pressure and slab stability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stepped spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"階梯混凝土接縫可能將表面動壓傳入底部，反覆升降的底板下壓力影響錨定與接觸。平均淨水頭只給靜態揚力量級，堵塞排水與脈動相關性需另考慮；驗證必須涵蓋接縫、底層與排水出口的連續水路。 驗證時應量測接縫兩側與底板下壓力並核對排水出口流量，並辨識以下失效情境：排水堵塞會讓接縫入水轉成持續底板揚壓。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「接縫滲壓與穩定」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Concrete joints can transmit surface pressure beneath stepped slabs and impose cyclic uplift. Mean differential head provides a static scale only; drain blockage and pressure correlation need separate treatment. Verification must trace the connected route through joints, the underlying layer and drainage outlets. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure pressures across joints and beneath slabs and check drainage outlet flow. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: A blocked drain converts joint inflow into sustained slab uplift. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Joint pressure and slab stability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：NetUnderSlabHead=1.5 m; slabArea=12 m2; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; uplift=1.5*12*9.81=176.58 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: NetUnderSlabHead=1.5 m; slabArea=12 m2; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; uplift=1.5*12*9.81=176.58 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「階梯表面耗能良好就代表底板不會受揚壓」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Effective surface dissipation means slabs cannot experience uplift\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「接縫滲壓與穩定」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Joint pressure and slab stability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-33-k1","title":"接縫滲壓與穩定","titleEn":"Joint pressure and slab stability","text":"階梯混凝土接縫可能將表面動壓傳入底部，反覆升降的底板下壓力影響錨定與接觸。平均淨水頭只給靜態揚力量級，堵塞排水與脈動相關性需另考慮；驗證必須涵蓋接縫、底層與排水出口的連續水路。","textEn":"Concrete joints can transmit surface pressure beneath stepped slabs and impose cyclic uplift. Mean differential head provides a static scale only; drain blockage and pressure correlation need separate treatment.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：階梯表面耗能良好就代表底板不會受揚壓 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Effective surface dissipation means slabs cannot experience uplift Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接縫滲壓與穩定」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joint pressure and slab stability\" is correct?","options":["階梯混凝土接縫可能將表面動壓傳入底部，反覆升降的底板下壓力影響錨定與接觸。","階梯表面耗能良好就代表底板不會受揚壓","相同福祿數也保證雷諾數自動相同"],"optionsEn":["Concrete joints can transmit surface pressure beneath stepped slabs and impose cyclic uplift.","Effective surface dissipation means slabs cannot experience uplift","Equal Froude numbers also guarantee equal Reynolds numbers"],"answer":0,"explanation":"階梯混凝土接縫可能將表面動壓傳入底部，反覆升降的底板下壓力影響錨定與接觸。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Concrete joints can transmit surface pressure beneath stepped slabs and impose cyclic uplift. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b246-v15-34","title":"接縫滲壓與穩定：定量估算","titleEn":"Joint pressure and slab stability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「接縫滲壓與穩定」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Joint pressure and slab stability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：NetUnderSlabHead=1.5 m; slabArea=12 m2; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; uplift=1.5*12*9.81=176.58 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: NetUnderSlabHead=1.5 m; slabArea=12 m2; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; uplift=1.5*12*9.81=176.58 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測接縫兩側與底板下壓力並核對排水出口流量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure pressures across joints and beneath slabs and check drainage outlet flow.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：NetUnderSlabHead=1.5 m; slabArea=12 m2; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; uplift=1.5*12*9.81=176.58 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: NetUnderSlabHead=1.5 m; slabArea=12 m2; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; uplift=1.5*12*9.81=176.58 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接縫滲壓與穩定」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joint pressure and slab stability\", which statement holds?","options":["同一水深階高比保證所有坡度流態相同","原創教學假設：NetUnderSlabHead=1.5 m; slabArea=12 m2; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; uplift=1.5*12*9.81=176.58 kN。","只要增加階數總耗能就能無限制線性增加"],"optionsEn":["The same relative depth guarantees the same regime on every slope","Original teaching assumptions: NetUnderSlabHead=1.5 m; slabArea=12 m2; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; uplift=1.5*12*9.81=176.58 kN.","Adding steps increases total dissipation linearly without limit"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：NetUnderSlabHead=1.5 m; slabArea=12 m2; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; uplift=1.5*12*9.81=176.58 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: NetUnderSlabHead=1.5 m; slabArea=12 m2; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; uplift=1.5*12*9.81=176.58 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b246-v15-35","title":"接縫滲壓與穩定：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joint pressure and slab stability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「接縫滲壓與穩定」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Joint pressure and slab stability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測接縫兩側與底板下壓力並核對排水出口流量。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「排水堵塞會讓接縫入水轉成持續底板揚壓」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure pressures across joints and beneath slabs and check drainage outlet flow. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A blocked drain converts joint inflow into sustained slab uplift. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以量測接縫兩側與底板下壓力並核對排水出口流量作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對排水堵塞會讓接縫入水轉成持續底板揚壓，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure pressures across joints and beneath slabs and check drainage outlet flow. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A blocked drain converts joint inflow into sustained slab uplift. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：排水堵塞會讓接縫入水轉成持續底板揚壓。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A blocked drain converts joint inflow into sustained slab uplift. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測接縫兩側與底板下壓力並核對排水出口流量。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「排水堵塞會讓接縫入水轉成持續底板揚壓」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure pressures across joints and beneath slabs and check drainage outlet flow. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A blocked drain converts joint inflow into sustained slab uplift. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以量測接縫兩側與底板下壓力並核對排水出口流量作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對排水堵塞會讓接縫入水轉成持續底板揚壓，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure pressures across joints and beneath slabs and check drainage outlet flow. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A blocked drain converts joint inflow into sustained slab uplift. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接縫滲壓與穩定」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joint pressure and slab stability\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","混合層厚度與清水等效深度永遠相同","量測接縫兩側與底板下壓力並核對排水出口流量。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Mixture thickness always equals clear-water equivalent depth","Measure pressures across joints and beneath slabs and check drainage outlet flow."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測接縫兩側與底板下壓力並核對排水出口流量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure pressures across joints and beneath slabs and check drainage outlet flow. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b246-v15-36","title":"接縫滲壓與穩定：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joint pressure and slab stability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「接縫滲壓與穩定」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Joint pressure and slab stability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"排水堵塞會讓接縫入水轉成持續底板揚壓。診斷時應採取以下查核：量測接縫兩側與底板下壓力並核對排水出口流量，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A blocked drain converts joint inflow into sustained slab uplift. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure pressures across joints and beneath slabs and check drainage outlet flow. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「階梯表面耗能良好就代表底板不會受揚壓」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Effective surface dissipation means slabs cannot experience uplift\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"排水堵塞會讓接縫入水轉成持續底板揚壓。診斷時應採取以下查核：量測接縫兩側與底板下壓力並核對排水出口流量，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"A blocked drain converts joint inflow into sustained slab uplift. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure pressures across joints and beneath slabs and check drainage outlet flow. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接縫滲壓與穩定」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joint pressure and slab stability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["排水堵塞會讓接縫入水轉成持續底板揚壓。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","相同福祿數也保證雷諾數自動相同"],"optionsEn":["A blocked drain converts joint inflow into sustained slab uplift.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Equal Froude numbers also guarantee equal Reynolds numbers"],"answer":0,"explanation":"排水堵塞會讓接縫入水轉成持續底板揚壓。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A blocked drain converts joint inflow into sustained slab uplift. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b246-v15-37","title":"縮尺黏性與可比性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Scale viscosity and comparability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「縮尺黏性與可比性」如何影響階梯式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Scale viscosity and comparability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stepped spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"同水質福祿模型的速度隨長度平方根縮小，使雷諾數比按長度比的二分之三次方改變。小模型可能改變階穴紊流與含氣，結果需附尺度限制；應分開驗證整體水面線與細部氣泡機制，不能用單一相似準則涵蓋所有現象。 驗證時應列出原型與模型雷諾數並比較兩種模型尺度的含氣結果，並辨識以下失效情境：模型黏性過強會改變階穴交換與表面擾動。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「縮尺黏性與可比性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"In a same-fluid Froude model, velocity scales with square root of length, making the Reynolds-number ratio length to the three-halves power. Small models may change cavity turbulence and aeration. Report scale limits and distinguish whole-profile validation from detailed bubble mechanisms rather than assuming universal similarity. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: List prototype and model Reynolds numbers and compare aeration at two model scales. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Excessive model viscosity changes cavity exchange and surface disturbance. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Scale viscosity and comparability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Prototype/model lengthRatio=20; same kinematicViscosity; ReynoldsRatio=20**1.5=89.4427 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Prototype/model lengthRatio=20; same kinematicViscosity; ReynoldsRatio=20**1.5=89.4427 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「相同福祿數也保證雷諾數自動相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal Froude numbers also guarantee equal Reynolds numbers\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「縮尺黏性與可比性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Scale viscosity and comparability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-37-k1","title":"縮尺黏性與可比性","titleEn":"Scale viscosity and comparability","text":"同水質福祿模型的速度隨長度平方根縮小，使雷諾數比按長度比的二分之三次方改變。小模型可能改變階穴紊流與含氣，結果需附尺度限制；應分開驗證整體水面線與細部氣泡機制，不能用單一相似準則涵蓋所有現象。","textEn":"In a same-fluid Froude model, velocity scales with square root of length, making the Reynolds-number ratio length to the three-halves power. Small models may change cavity turbulence and aeration.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：相同福祿數也保證雷諾數自動相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal Froude numbers also guarantee equal Reynolds numbers Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「縮尺黏性與可比性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Scale viscosity and comparability\" is correct?","options":["相同福祿數也保證雷諾數自動相同","同水質福祿模型的速度隨長度平方根縮小，使雷諾數比按長度比的二分之三次方改變。","臨界水深就是每一階上的實際水深"],"optionsEn":["Equal Froude numbers also guarantee equal Reynolds numbers","In a same-fluid Froude model, velocity scales with square root of length, making the Reynolds-number ratio length to the three-halves power.","Critical depth equals actual flow depth on every step"],"answer":1,"explanation":"同水質福祿模型的速度隨長度平方根縮小，使雷諾數比按長度比的二分之三次方改變。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"In a same-fluid Froude model, velocity scales with square root of length, making the Reynolds-number ratio length to the three-halves power. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b246-v15-38","title":"縮尺黏性與可比性：定量估算","titleEn":"Scale viscosity and comparability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「縮尺黏性與可比性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Scale viscosity and comparability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Prototype/model lengthRatio=20; same kinematicViscosity; ReynoldsRatio=20**1.5=89.4427 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Prototype/model lengthRatio=20; same kinematicViscosity; ReynoldsRatio=20**1.5=89.4427 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：列出原型與模型雷諾數並比較兩種模型尺度的含氣結果。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: List prototype and model Reynolds numbers and compare aeration at two model scales.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Prototype/model lengthRatio=20; same kinematicViscosity; ReynoldsRatio=20**1.5=89.4427 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Prototype/model lengthRatio=20; same kinematicViscosity; ReynoldsRatio=20**1.5=89.4427 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「縮尺黏性與可比性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Scale viscosity and comparability\", which statement holds?","options":["平均坡度正確就不必檢查個別階梯","表面變白就保證底部已獲充分含氣保護","原創教學假設：Prototype/model lengthRatio=20; same kinematicViscosity; ReynoldsRatio=20**1.5=89.4427 dimensionless。"],"optionsEn":["Correct average slope removes the need to inspect individual steps","A white surface guarantees adequate air protection at the bed","Original teaching assumptions: Prototype/model lengthRatio=20; same kinematicViscosity; ReynoldsRatio=20**1.5=89.4427 dimensionless."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Prototype/model lengthRatio=20; same kinematicViscosity; ReynoldsRatio=20**1.5=89.4427 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Prototype/model lengthRatio=20; same kinematicViscosity; ReynoldsRatio=20**1.5=89.4427 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b246-v15-39","title":"縮尺黏性與可比性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Scale viscosity and comparability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「縮尺黏性與可比性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Scale viscosity and comparability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"列出原型與模型雷諾數並比較兩種模型尺度的含氣結果。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「模型黏性過強會改變階穴交換與表面擾動」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"List prototype and model Reynolds numbers and compare aeration at two model scales. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Excessive model viscosity changes cavity exchange and surface disturbance. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以列出原型與模型雷諾數並比較兩種模型尺度的含氣結果作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對模型黏性過強會改變階穴交換與表面擾動，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: List prototype and model Reynolds numbers and compare aeration at two model scales. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Excessive model viscosity changes cavity exchange and surface disturbance. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：模型黏性過強會改變階穴交換與表面擾動。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Excessive model viscosity changes cavity exchange and surface disturbance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"列出原型與模型雷諾數並比較兩種模型尺度的含氣結果。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「模型黏性過強會改變階穴交換與表面擾動」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"List prototype and model Reynolds numbers and compare aeration at two model scales. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Excessive model viscosity changes cavity exchange and surface disturbance. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以列出原型與模型雷諾數並比較兩種模型尺度的含氣結果作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對模型黏性過強會改變階穴交換與表面擾動，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: List prototype and model Reynolds numbers and compare aeration at two model scales. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Excessive model viscosity changes cavity exchange and surface disturbance. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「縮尺黏性與可比性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Scale viscosity and comparability\"?","options":["列出原型與模型雷諾數並比較兩種模型尺度的含氣結果。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","表壓可直接與絕對蒸氣壓相減"],"optionsEn":["List prototype and model Reynolds numbers and compare aeration at two model scales.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Gauge pressure can be subtracted directly from absolute vapor pressure"],"answer":0,"explanation":"列出原型與模型雷諾數並比較兩種模型尺度的含氣結果。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"List prototype and model Reynolds numbers and compare aeration at two model scales. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b246-v15-40","title":"縮尺黏性與可比性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Scale viscosity and comparability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b246-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「縮尺黏性與可比性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Scale viscosity and comparability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"模型黏性過強會改變階穴交換與表面擾動。診斷時應採取以下查核：列出原型與模型雷諾數並比較兩種模型尺度的含氣結果，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Excessive model viscosity changes cavity exchange and surface disturbance. Diagnose it by the following check: List prototype and model Reynolds numbers and compare aeration at two model scales. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「相同福祿數也保證雷諾數自動相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal Froude numbers also guarantee equal Reynolds numbers\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b246-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"模型黏性過強會改變階穴交換與表面擾動。診斷時應採取以下查核：列出原型與模型雷諾數並比較兩種模型尺度的含氣結果，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Excessive model viscosity changes cavity exchange and surface disturbance. Diagnose it by the following check: List prototype and model Reynolds numbers and compare aeration at two model scales. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]},{"id":"b246-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「縮尺黏性與可比性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Scale viscosity and comparability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","模型黏性過強會改變階穴交換與表面擾動。","臨界水深就是每一階上的實際水深"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Excessive model viscosity changes cavity exchange and surface disturbance.","Critical depth equals actual flow depth on every step"],"answer":1,"explanation":"模型黏性過強會改變階穴交換與表面擾動。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Excessive model viscosity changes cavity exchange and surface disturbance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-stepped","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
